%N A400098 Numbers k such that the trajectory of k->ord(5,k) reaches 1 before reaching a number not coprime to 5. Here ord(b,k) is the multiplicative order of b modulo k.
%C A400098 Closed under multiplication.
%C A400098 Also numbers k such that the trajectory of k->ord(-5,k) reaches 1 before reaching a number not coprime to -5. See A400096 for general discussions.
%H A400098 Jianing Song, <a href="/A400098/b400098.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A400098 Powers of 2 are terms: 2^n -> 2^(n-2) -> 2^(n-4) -> ... -> 2 or 1;
%e A400098 19 is a term: 19 -> 9 -> 6 -> 2 -> 1.
%t A400098 (* okQ is defined at A400096 *)
%t A400098 Select[Range[120], okQ[#, 5] &] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Nov 26 2026 *)
%o A400098 (PARI) isok(n, 5) \\ see A400096 for isok
%Y A400098 See A400096 for list of sequences in other bases.
%K A400098 nonn,new
%O A400098 1,2
%A A400098 _Jianing Song_, Nov 24 2026
